    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Substitute $u=\\ln x+\\frac1x$",
        "body": "Rewrite $\\frac{x-1}{x^2\\ln x+x}=\\frac{(x-1)/x^2}{\\ln x+\\frac1x}$. With $u=\\ln x+\\frac1x$ we have $du=\\left(\\frac1x-\\frac1{x^2}\\right)dx=\\frac{x-1}{x^2}dx$. At $x=1$, $u=1$; at $x=2$, $u=\\ln2+\\frac12$. So the integral is $\\int_1^{\\ln2+1/2}\\frac{du}u=\\ln\\left(\\tfrac12+\\ln2\\right)$.\n\n**Answer: $\\ln\\left(\\frac12+\\ln 2\\right)$**"
      }
    ],
